---
// The masthead + the single most persuasive object on the page: a rendered
// product surface refusing to guess. Evolved into a "record entry" to fit the
// field-journal identity. No competitor's landing page can show a refusal.
---

<section id="top" class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <!-- journal masthead -->
  <div class="shell">
    <div
      class="rise flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-1 border-b border-line py-3 font-mono text-[0.68rem] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-faint"
    >
      <span class="text-accent">Healthee</span>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span>An honest health companion</span>
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="hidden sm:inline">/</span>
      <span class="hidden sm:inline">Self-hosted &middot; grounded in graded research</span>
      <span class="ml-auto hidden md:inline">Edition 2026&middot;07</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="shell grid items-end gap-14 pt-14 pb-16 md:pt-20 md:pb-20 lg:grid-cols-[1.06fr_0.94fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow rise">The health app that marks its own work</p>

      <h1 class="rise mt-6 text-[clamp(2.6rem,6.4vw,4.9rem)]">
        Every claim it makes<br class="hidden sm:block" />
        is <span class="italic text-accent-soft">cited</span>, or it
        <span class="italic text-accent-soft">doesn&rsquo;t ship.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="rise mt-7 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Healthee reads your wearable and tells you the truth: every interpretation footnoted to
        graded research<sup class="ref"><a href="#ref-9" aria-label="reference 9">9</a></sup>, every
        number carrying its own confidence, and
        <span class="text-ink">&ldquo;not enough data&rdquo;</span> whenever that is the honest
        answer. No green rings. No grading on a curve.
      </p>

      <div class="rise mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a href="#self-host" class="btn btn-primary">Self-host it today</a>
        <a href="#coach" class="btn btn-ghost">Read a real coach reply &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p class="rise mt-6 max-w-md text-sm text-ink-faint">
        You own the hardware and the data. You pay only for the intelligence &mdash; and only if you
        want it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- the refusal, as a record entry -->
    <div class="rise lg:justify-self-end">
      <figure
        class="surface w-full max-w-md p-6 sm:p-7"
        aria-label="Rendered example: the product declining to score on insufficient data"
      >
        <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
          <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
            Record &middot; recovery &middot; today
          </span>
          <span class="chip chip-gold chip-dot">not enough data</span>
        </figcaption>

        <hr class="hairline my-5" />

        <p class="font-serif text-[1.7rem] leading-snug">
          I&rsquo;m not going to give you a recovery score today.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Only <span class="mono text-ink">2</span> of the last
          <span class="mono text-ink">7</span> nights have usable overnight HRV. A recovery number
          needs a stable baseline; inventing one would be worse than staying quiet.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <span class="chip">coverage&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;29%</span>
          <span class="chip">baseline&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;insufficient</span>
          <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">fix&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;wear 5+ nights</span>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <p class="mono mt-3 pl-1 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        A rendered example of the honesty contract, not a live reading.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- honest status ribbon -->
  <div class="shell">
    <div
      class="rise flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 border-y border-line py-4 text-sm text-ink-soft"
    >
      <span class="eyebrow">Where it stands</span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">live</span> Backend: deployed &amp; multi-tenant
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="chip chip-dot">building</span> Mobile app: in progress (Phase 2)
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="chip chip-dot">closed</span> Public sign-ups: not open yet
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
